+## 8. Addendum (2026-09-06, post-PR): CI red on PR #431 — root cause and fix
+
+**Symptom:** the “Test Suite” job failed at the new
+“Differential fuzz smoke (synthetic)” step (run 34061832519) with exit 1;
+Clippy and every earlier step (build, `cargo test`, regression corpus,
+engine guard) were green.
+
+**Root cause (reproduced deterministically):** `fuzz_diff.py` validated
+`--lccc` against the launcher’s CWD but executed each compile from a
+per-case **temporary directory**. CI passes the relative path
+`target/fastbuild/lccc`; from the tempdir that is ENOENT, which the harness
+classified as `LCCC_CRASH` → exit 1. Every seed fails with a relative
+`--lccc` and none with an absolute one — the time-based default seed only
+made it look random.
+
+**Fix (commit `929ba8f1`):** `main()` resolves `--lccc` and every `--refs`
+entry to an absolute spelling once (shutil.which for PATH names,
+`Path.resolve()` for files) before any evaluation, making every engine
+CWD-independent; missing references are reported instead of silently
+dropped. The CI smoke now pins `--seed 20260906` so failures are exactly
+reproducible (the default was time-based — a smoke that tests different
+programs every run cannot be debugged from a red check).
+
+**Validation:** exact CI command (relative path) 4/4 PASS; pinned seed 4/4
+vs gcc and vs gcc+clang at `-O0..-O3`; 20-seed sweep (relative paths,
+gcc+clang, `-O0,-O2`) all PASS; csmith 2/2, stress_suite 4/4,
+`--check-engines` 4/4, legacy wrapper translation verified. The three CI
+steps that never ran on the failed PR job (inline-asm UTF-8,
+strict computed-reciprocal codegen, MachInst window allocation) pass
+locally against the fixed tree, so the full job is expected green.
+
+**Lesson:** when a tool executes subprocesses with a different CWD than the
+one that validated the inputs, resolve every path at the boundary — before
+the first fork. And a CI smoke must be deterministic: pin the seed.
